      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I don’t see an issue with this, since instance naming is purely cosmetic. While named instances might look appealing, group instances can be considered even more attractive. It’s also worth noting that not every user can create groups, and many groups restrict instance creation altogether — meaning there are already barriers in place for free users to creating 'attractive' instances.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2025-09-05T03:50:29.783Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I don't think the ability to name instances should be locked behind VRC+.\n\nNamed public instances are far more attractive to players than unnamed ones, which means non-subscribers will be discouraged from making their own instances. This is already somewhat proven by the popularity of Group Public instances, not because the groups are moderating them (they rarely are), but simply because players like the names associated with these instances.\n\nAdditionally, by locking naming behind VRC+, non-subscribers are encouraged to use awkward workarounds like using the API or editing website links. This creates an unnecessary barrier for regular players and makes the feature feel incomplete.\n\nSince instance naming will be widespread and an objective improvement over the old system, it feels wrong to treat it as a premium perk rather than a core upgrade available to everyone.",
